{"data":{"featured":{"edges":[{"node":{"frontmatter":{"title":"OpenClimateFix Weather Pipeline","cover":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/26b2068fa7371c8b81a6462ebe66c73e/be5ed/cover.jpg","srcSet":"/static/26b2068fa7371c8b81a6462ebe66c73e/8bb35/cover.jpg 125w,\n/static/26b2068fa7371c8b81a6462ebe66c73e/f505e/cover.jpg 250w,\n/static/26b2068fa7371c8b81a6462ebe66c73e/be5ed/cover.jpg 500w","sizes":"(min-width: 500px) 500px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/26b2068fa7371c8b81a6462ebe66c73e/3ebc4/cover.avif 125w,\n/static/26b2068fa7371c8b81a6462ebe66c73e/a9ff4/cover.avif 250w,\n/static/26b2068fa7371c8b81a6462ebe66c73e/a61b1/cover.avif 500w","type":"image/avif","sizes":"(min-width: 500px) 500px, 100vw"},{"srcSet":"/static/26b2068fa7371c8b81a6462ebe66c73e/d66e1/cover.webp 125w,\n/static/26b2068fa7371c8b81a6462ebe66c73e/e7160/cover.webp 250w,\n/static/26b2068fa7371c8b81a6462ebe66c73e/5f169/cover.webp 500w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 500px) 500px, 100vw"}]},"width":700,"height":700}}},"tech":["Python","Apache Airflow","PyTorch","Graph Neural Networks","Apache Kafka"],"github":"https://github.com/openclimatefix","external":"https://openclimatefix.org/","cta":""},"html":"<p>OpenClimateFix builds open-source ML for solar power forecasting, and better forecasts mean grid operators burn less gas covering for cloudy afternoons. I contribute to the weather side of that.</p>\n<p>My patches live in three places: validation pipelines in Airflow that keep bad sensor data out of training, anomaly detection that flags suspicious readings before they poison a model, and distributed-training work that makes the GNN forecasting models cheaper to iterate on.</p>"}},{"node":{"frontmatter":{"title":"AI Ticket Triage, Fully Local","cover":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/d2194/cover.png","srcSet":"/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/cebcc/cover.png 175w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/272cf/cover.png 350w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/d2194/cover.png 700w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/b50c4/cover.png 1400w","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/9aa63/cover.avif 175w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/e6db6/cover.avif 350w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/f47db/cover.avif 700w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/8fee6/cover.avif 1400w","type":"image/avif","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},{"srcSet":"/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/240e7/cover.webp 175w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/faefe/cover.webp 350w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/d5dc4/cover.webp 700w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/e2f1a/cover.webp 1400w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"}]},"width":700,"height":438}}},"tech":["LangGraph","Ollama","Qwen3","FastAPI","LangSmith"],"github":"https://github.com/glitch401/p1-seafoam-cicada","external":"https://github.com/glitch401/p1-seafoam-cicada","cta":""},"html":"<p>Support queues die by a thousand lookups: find the order, check the policy, draft the reply. This agent does the boring parts, and it does them without sending a single byte to the cloud.</p>\n<p>LangGraph manages state through sticky threads that pin each conversation to its Order ID, Qwen3 runs locally over Ollama, and every decision is traced in LangSmith so I can see exactly why the agent wrote what it wrote. A Next.js chat UI sits on top.</p>"}}]}}}